#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:10
msgid "Scope and method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 30 files (3,964 lines; 178,026 bytes): 16 "
"filing/workflow skills and form-orientation companions, harness resource "
"and metadata loaders, workspace/plugin materialization, and the MCP "
"protocol/runtime adapter. I read every assigned range from the chunk "
"reader, including all eight pages. This is static inspection only; no "
"application, MCP server, or filing workflow was run. The `SKILL.md` and "
"companion Markdown files are bundled operator guidance, not executable "
"tax logic. Their claims about rules, registry content, and workflow "
"outcomes are not independently validated here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:14
msgid "User-facing capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:16
msgid ""
"The model-specific skills present a repeatable filing lifecycle—check "
"applicability and source records, inspect the registry shape, create a "
"work unit, calculate, inspect the revision and notices, verify, export a "
"local artifact, and reconcile only after the taxpayer files. Across the "
"reviewed files they repeatedly tell the operator to relay CLI values and "
"legal/source references rather than hand-calculate casillas, and to "
"distinguish a local export from AEAT acceptance. That makes the skills "
"useful as interaction policy and sequencing aids, while the calculation "
"and authority remain in the underlying CLI and registry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:18
msgid ""
"The IVA coverage in this chunk is deliberately differentiated. Modelo 309"
" is an ad-hoc, non-periodic IVA obligation using `AD-HOC`; the skill "
"distinguishes its triggering events from a periodic Modelo 303 and "
"describes two ledger-bound leaves and one computed total. Modelo 322 is "
"the monthly individual filing of an IVA group member, while Modelo 353 is"
" the dominant entity's monthly group filing. The 322 guidance warns "
"against presenting one member's result as the group result; the 353 guide"
" separates directly calculated dominant-entity ledger casillas from three"
" evolving cross-member reconciliation casillas and says to inspect "
"dependency clean-state before treating the latter as a complete group "
"cross-check. The 353 companion page likewise warns that the "
"reconciliation values depend on a complete member roster and captured "
"member observations. See the 309 skill "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-309/SKILL.md`), 322 skill and casilla orientation "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-322/SKILL.md`), and 353 skill and casilla orientation "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-353/SKILL.md`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:20
msgid ""
"Modelo 349 is framed correctly as an informational recapitulativa without"
" a tax-due/refund result. Its guide explains direction-specific "
"collectible/payable invoice sourcing, operator and rectification rows, "
"the cadence switch between monthly and quarterly periods, and a separate "
"comparison with the period's 303. Modelo 369 has three distinct schemas "
"selected by the period-token family: quarterly Unión, `EXT-` quarterly "
"Exterior, and monthly Importación/IOSS. It directs operators to prepare "
"each applicable scheme as an independent work unit. Modelo 390 is an "
"annual summary that reconciles annual ledger totals against four prior "
"quarterly 303s, including a blocking equality gate and special carry-"
"forward casilla treatment. The companion pages repeatedly label their "
"listed casillas as orientation, directing users to the year/period "
"registry output as canonical. These are useful guardrails, but the legal "
"accuracy and agreement with current registry revisions require separate "
"validation. See the 349 material (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills"
"/cadrumo-preparar-modelo-349/SKILL.md`), 369 material "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-369/SKILL.md`), and 390 skill "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-390/SKILL.md`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:22
msgid ""
"The broader itineraries handle cross-cutting situations rather than "
"owning calculations. The Sociedad guide derives obligations from "
"calendar/agenda/explain output and sequences per-modelo skills; the "
"employer/withholder guide overlays labor, professional-fee, and rental "
"withholding facts without replacing the taxpayer's primary regime route. "
"The annual-window guide orders annual summaries before annual returns and"
" routes missing quarters to the overdue workflow. The arrears guide uses "
"the CLI backlog and recargo outputs, keeps cases oldest-first, "
"distinguishes missed filings from amendments, and diverts cases with an "
"AEAT requerimiento to a human professional. The rectification guide "
"requires official evidence for the prior filing and source-level "
"correction before amendment; reconciliation explicitly refuses to equate "
"a local export with acceptance. These prompts encode conservative "
"handoffs and keep human filing/reconciliation visible. See Sociedad "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-pyme-"
"sociedad/SKILL.md`), withholding (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills"
"/cadrumo-retenedor-empleador/SKILL.md`), annual window "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-resumen-"
"anual/SKILL.md`), arrears (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills"
"/cadrumo-regularizar-atrasos/SKILL.md`), amendments "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-rectificar-"
"declaracion/SKILL.md`), and reconciliation "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-reconciliar/SKILL.md`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:24
msgid "Selection, resources, and materialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:26
msgid ""
"The harness provides a structured `applies_when` schema over profile "
"facts, workflow phase, and temporal triggers. Fact names and enum values "
"are derived from the live `TaxpayerProfile` model, including one nested "
"level, rather than copied into a separate hand-maintained list. Frozen, "
"extra-forbidden Pydantic models validate match modes, value shapes, enum "
"membership, and the exclusive `always=true` form. YAML frontmatter is "
"parsed with `safe_load`; the resource iterator verifies each parsed skill"
" name matches its directory. One deliberate boundary remains: "
"`SkillMetadata.applies_when` is optional at parse time, and the docstring"
" assigns strict “every skill has a predicate” coverage to a separate "
"gate. Calling the loader alone therefore does not prove complete "
"selection metadata. See `_skill_metadata.py` "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_skill_metadata.py`) and `resources.py` "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/resources.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:28
msgid ""
"Resource access uses `importlib.resources` `Traversable` paths rooted in "
"the installed package, so the harness can read bundled resources without "
"assuming a checkout layout. The workspace writer emits Claude-native "
"rules, persona files, skills, a root `CLAUDE.md` importing the rules, or "
"a plugin package with MCP configuration. Persona frontmatter carries a "
"derived description; read-only personas have edit/write tools disallowed,"
" while mutating personas rely on the runtime-grant model. The plugin path"
" validates a bundled wheel cohort and its manifest/digests before "
"producing an offline `uvx` invocation with ambient Python settings "
"constrained; the required package version is also checked by the MCP "
"entrypoint when configured. This reduces dependence on an index or an "
"unrelated installed checkout. Materialization writes into caller-selected"
" output directories, and plugin regeneration clears the designated "
"artifact directory; callers must treat that destination as an explicit "
"filesystem trust boundary. See `_workspace.py` plugin launch and cohort "
"handling (`src/cadrumo_harness/_workspace.py`), plugin materialization "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_workspace.py`), workspace materialization "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_workspace.py`), and `_resources.py` "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_resources.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:30
msgid ""
"One bounded extensibility caveat is visible in `_copy_skill`: its "
"docstring says “whole subtree,” but the implementation copies direct "
"files and then files in each immediate child directory; it does not "
"recursively descend into grandchildren. The reviewed companion references"
" are one level below their skill directories, so this does not establish "
"current data loss in this chunk. A future nested resource could be "
"omitted from a materialized workspace unless the traversal becomes "
"recursive or the supported layout is explicitly constrained. See "
"`_copy_skill` (`src/cadrumo_harness/_workspace.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:32
msgid "MCP protocol and trust boundaries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:34
msgid ""
"The MCP server advertises a stable 15-tool catalogue spanning "
"unauthenticated status, enrollment/authentication, public authority "
"queries, and admitted operation "
"search/description/submission/observation/results/review/control. The "
"protocol boundary rejects missing, extra, mistyped, and out-of-enum "
"fields; integer checks explicitly exclude booleans. Tool schemas use "
"`additionalProperties: false`. The authority tool has conditional "
"coordinates: a second query-specific validator rejects coordinates that "
"are not allowed or required for that query and bounds filing year, while "
"the query executes under one `bundled_indexed_authority().operation()` "
"and returns its logical generation and reader incarnation. This pins each"
" response to a publication generation; it does not itself establish the "
"legal correctness of the bundled authority. See `protocol_contract.py` "
"catalogue and validation (`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/protocol_contract.py`)"
" and `authority_query.py` (`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/authority_query.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:36
msgid ""
"The runtime adapter binds one connection to one immutable profile and an "
"optional MCP frontend client. Admission checks require the client "
"profile/frontend to match, a live grant and unexpired session, and a "
"connected/authenticated/profile-bound status whose profile and session "
"IDs match the client. Calls are serialized per adapter; blocking runtime "
"work is sent to a thread with cancellation-complete cleanup. "
"Authentication opens a protected credential reference, verifies exact "
"admitted status, then retires the prior client after replacement. "
"Enrollment is a separate per-connection door: it allows one pending "
"request/proposal at a time, checks expiry/completion before replacement, "
"supports rotation reconciliation through a credential reference, and "
"returns projections rather than raw credential material. See "
"`runtime_admission.py` (`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/runtime_admission.py`) "
"and `runtime_adapter.py` admission/enrollment "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/runtime_adapter.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:38
msgid ""
"Admitted operation dispatch delegates to typed runtime requests. "
"Submission uses a generated request ID, the bound profile/session, "
"caller-provided subject and payload, and optional idempotency key; JSON "
"serialization forbids NaN. On a refusal, timeout, or connection close "
"after submission, the adapter returns an unresolved outcome with the "
"request ID and definition ID rather than claiming failure erased the "
"submission. If an automatic start fails after a durable receipt, that "
"receipt remains in the response. Result and page reads use typed "
"projection requests; response management binds actor identity to the "
"admitted session, and cancel/detach require a revision. The public result"
" classifier recognizes explicit refusal envelopes and only treats a "
"result page as a refusal when it is a complete, digest-matching canonical"
" refusal document, avoiding classification of an arbitrary partial page "
"as one. See `admitted_operations.py` "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/admitted_operations.py`), "
"`protocol_contract.py` refusal classification "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/protocol_contract.py`), and `server.py` "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/server.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:40
msgid ""
"Cleanup ownership is connection-scoped: adapter close retires its "
"admitted/enrollment clients and retained failed-admission cleanup owners,"
" while the server docstring states that EOF does not close the shared "
"runtime. The outer serving wrapper releases the bundled authority after "
"normal transport return. This separation is appropriate for concurrent "
"clients; actual retry behavior and transport lifecycle outcomes were not "
"exercised. The CLI entrypoint accepts a profile UUID and optional "
"credential-reference UUID, can enforce the installed cohort version, "
"configures logging, and reports a missing MCP SDK. The source inspected "
"here does not establish the host OS's protection of process arguments; "
"deployment should keep the referenced credential protected independently."
" See `runtime_cleanup.py` (`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/runtime_cleanup.py`),"
" `server.py` lifecycle (`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/server.py`), and "
"`main.py` (`src/cadrumo_harness/mcp/main.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:42
msgid "Assessment and bounded follow-up"
msgstr "Evaluación y seguimiento acotado"

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:44
msgid ""
"The strongest implementation contribution is the typed, connection-owned "
"MCP adapter around existing runtime contracts: exact-profile lease "
"admission, one publication pin for authority reads, retained submission "
"receipts for uncertain outcomes, and explicit cleanup ownership. The "
"prompt layer complements it with careful separation of applicability, "
"calculation, verification, local export, and official reconciliation. "
"These boundaries improve explainability and reduce operator "
"improvisation; they are not a substitute for validating the legal content"
" or end-to-end authority of the underlying domain layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/187-filing-skills-and-the-mcp-operator-harness.md:46
msgid ""
"For synthesis, verify three bounded questions against their owning "
"layers: (1) whether every referenced CLI command and per-modelo workflow "
"is present and whether the described registry bindings/equality gates "
"match implementation; (2) how current plugin callers constrain "
"output/artifact paths before the workspace writer clears them; and (3) "
"whether cancellation/cleanup ownership is exercised through server "
"shutdown and uncertain submission paths. The static files establish "
"interfaces and intended safeguards, not their runtime success. No "
"vulnerability or legal defect is asserted from the prompt text alone."
msgstr ""

